in a [Abm]honky-tonk, down in [Ebm]Mexico
He wears a [Ebm]purple sash, and a [Abm]black moustache, 
in a honky-tonk, down in [Ebm]Mexico
 
Verse 2:
The [Ebm]first time that I saw him, 
he was sittin' on a piano stool, I said, 
"Tell me, man, when does the fun begin?"
He just [Bb7]winked his eye and said "Man, be cool."
 
Chorus 2:
